 "news": {
  "date": "2026-09-25",
  "asof": "2026-09-28 16:15 UTC",
  "headline": "Bernstein de-rated the sector two days after Oktane \u2014 and the ten-year made its fourth straight high anyway",
  "standfirst": "Bernstein\u2019s Peter Weed downgraded Palo Alto, Okta and SentinelOne together, arguing the group had gotten over its skis with several names up roughly 100% this year. Zscaler \u2014 named in Okta\u2019s own Blueprint Alliance two days earlier \u2014 fell 8.64%, and OKTA fell 5.54% to 195.19, closing at its low and giving back two thirds of the Oktane gain. The rest of the market went the other way on a Trump-Xi meeting and the trade talks that followed: the Dow rose 0.93%, the S&P 0.51% to 7,743.41, and AAPL rose 1.53% to 341.07, its best close since entry. The ten-year reached 5.225%, its highest since 2007 and a fourth consecutive fresh high, with equities rising into it for a second session. Crude eased 1.82% to $92.89, down 7.8% on the week. GOOG added 0.61% and holds +0.75R. Every position is green, the nearest stop 9.5% away. Heat 3.05R against 3.0R, unchanged for two weeks.",
